moving between two locations.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.170
So how we first authenticate
the endpoints, encrypt the data,

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.730
validate that transaction,
and decrypt that data

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:11.590
once it's been moved around.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:16.479
So Google uses RSA 2048-bit
certificates to our front end.

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:17.770
We use perfect forward secrecy.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.950
We were the first major provider
to use perfect forward secrecy

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.299
